From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 21:32:54 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Meridian: the Workbench can list its sessions as chats, each
 with its status from Claude Code's hooks, and one mark on its sidebar row

A preview the Workbench page turns on (Customize > Advanced > Chats list).
Mission Control keeps, per Workbench that lists its sessions, the session on
screen and the list's order: a turn that ends (Stop) in a session not on
screen is "done, not seen" until shown. Snapshot nodes get "chat"
(needs / working / done / idle, '' without hooks) and "unseen"; the
snapshot gets "chats" per Workbench tab. The Workbench page gets each
terminal's state with its mission message while it lists them. The
sidebar's row of such a Workbench tab shows one mark: orange with a count
when sessions need you, else blue with a count, else a spinner; a click
while one needs you opens it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
